==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|stube}}, from {{inh|de|goh|stuba}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|stoof}}. Further origin uncertain. See {{m|en|stove}} for more.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃtuːbə/|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Stuben|Stübchen|dim2=Stüblein}}

# {{lb|de|regional}} [[living room]]
# [[room]] {{gloss|room used for a special purpose; the term is often found in compounds with somewhat old-fashioned character}}
# [[parlour]] {{gloss|a room used chiefly for representation purposes; often called {{m|de|gute Stube}} or the like}}
# the [[heated]] part of a traditional [[farmhouse]] (as opposed to stables, kitchen, etc.)
# {{lb|de|military}} [[bedroom]] in a [[barracks]]

